<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-24, alongside the Status__c value-set changes adding Prepare, Review and
        Approved (see that field's own comment). PURPOSE: Status__c now carries up to nine
        granular values across two record types, which is too fine-grained for a compact display
        surface (a list view column, a dashboard tile, a kanban-style board). This field collapses
        every Status__c value onto a four-step DISPLAY lifecycle: Not Sent, Sent, Signed, Declined.

        NAMED Tracking_Status__c, NOT Status_Summary__c or NDA_Stage__c - '_Status__c' suffix per
        ARCHITECTURE.md's status-field convention (a field expressing CURRENT STATE), and
        'Tracking' distinguishes it from the master Status__c it derives from without implying a
        Path-driving Stage__c (it drives no Path and gates nothing).

        EVERY Status__c VALUE MUST MAP - a CASE with no fallback would render BLANK for any value
        it does not name, which reads as a bug, not as "unmapped". The mapping:
          - Prepare, Approved, Not Sent, Pending          -> "Not Sent"  (document not yet sent)
            (⚠ this line read "Prepare, Review, Approved, Not Sent, Pending" until 2026-08-25 -
             see the amendment at the foot of this comment)
          - Sent                                          -> "Sent"
          - Received                                      -> "Sent"     (see note below - DECISION,
                                                                          not an accident)
          - Signed                                        -> "Signed"
          - Declined                                       -> "Declined"
          - anything else (a future Status__c value added without updating this formula)
                                                            -> "Not Sent" (explicit fallback, see
                                                                           below)

        Received -> "Sent" IS A DELIBERATE DECISION, STATED HERE PER THE TASK THAT ADDED THIS
        FIELD, NOT AN OVERSIGHT. Received is Acquisition_NDA-only (the broker's NDA has arrived at
        DPEG but is not yet DPEG's own signed copy going back out). On the four-step display scale
        this reads closer to "the document is in motion / out" than to "not yet sent", so it maps
        to Sent rather than Not Sent. This mirrors how Days_Out__c and the Acquisition_NDA record
        type's own 2026-08-16 reorder already treat 'Sent' as the acquisition-side terminal/active
        state - see that RecordType file's comment for the fuller reasoning on the acquisition
        sequence shape.

        FALLBACK IS "Not Sent", NOT "Signed" OR BLANK - fail-CLOSED by design, matching how
        NDA_Signed_Rollup's own default branch treats any unrecognised Status__c value as
        outstanding rather than complete (see that flow and Status__c's 2026-08-24 comment).
        Reaching the fallback means a new Status__c value was added to the picklist without this
        formula being updated to name it explicitly - that is a defect to fix (add the value to
        the CASE), not a state this field is meant to represent long-term.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-25 - 'Not Sent' IS NO LONGER A REACHABLE Status__c VALUE. THE FORMULA
        BELOW IS UNCHANGED AND MUST STAY UNCHANGED, INCLUDING ITS "Not Sent" LINE AND ITS
        "Not Sent" FALLBACK.
        =====================================================================

        The user removed 'Not Sent' from the Disposition_NDA record type in Setup (repo caught up
        the same day; the measured value list is in that record type file's own 2026-08-25
        amendment). Acquisition_NDA had already restricted it out, so 'Not Sent' is now on NO
        record type and cannot be WRITTEN on either - it stays ACTIVE on the master value set only
        so rows that already carry it keep working.

        WHAT DID NOT CHANGE, AND WHY THAT IS THE POINT: this field's SOURCE value 'Not Sent' is now
        legacy-only, but this field's DISPLAY value "Not Sent" is not - Prepare, Review and Approved
        all still collapse into it, and they are now the ONLY way a new disposition NDA reaches that
        bucket. (⚠ 'Review' left that list later the same day - see the foot of this comment.) The mapping line "Not Sent" -> "Not Sent" is kept for the rows that predate the
        removal, and the fallback is kept for the reason stated above. Deleting either would blank
        the display for real rows in usman-dpeg.

        ⚠ THE MAPPING TABLE ABOVE STILL READS "Prepare, Approved, Not Sent, Pending". That
        list is accurate as a description of the FORMULA. It is no longer a description of what a
        NEW record can be in - only Prepare and Approved are reachable on a disposition
        NDA, and only Pending on an acquisition one.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-25, LATER THE SAME DAY - THE "Review" BRANCH IS DELETED FROM THE CASE.
        THIS IS THE OPPOSITE TREATMENT TO THE "Not Sent" BRANCH IMMEDIATELY ABOVE, AND THE REASON
        IS EVIDENCE, NOT A CHANGE OF PRINCIPLE.
        =====================================================================

        The user removed 'Review' from the Disposition_NDA record type in Setup hours after adding
        it (measured value list: recordTypes/Disposition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml's second
        2026-08-25 amendment). Like 'Not Sent', it stays ACTIVE on the master value set and is now
        on NO record type, so it is UNWRITABLE on either type.

        WHY 'Not Sent' KEPT ITS BRANCH AND 'Review' DID NOT. The 'Not Sent' branch is kept for the
        rows that already carry the value. A live aggregate on 2026-08-25 measured the org and
        found ZERO rows at 'Review' on EITHER record type - the value was reachable for about one
        day - so the branch protects nothing. (The same aggregate found zero rows at 'Not Sent'
        too, contradicting the paragraph above; that branch was left in place rather than
        re-litigated, and the correction is recorded in RecordStageAdvanceService's
        NDA_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE comment.)

        🔴 DELETING THIS BRANCH IS A BEHAVIOURAL NO-OP AND THAT IS THE POINT. "Review" mapped to
        the "Not Sent" DISPLAY bucket, and the CASE's explicit fallback is also "Not Sent" - so a
        row that somehow carried 'Review' renders identically before and after. Nothing about the
        display changes; what changes is that this file stops naming a value the process no longer
        has. Do not "restore it for completeness": under the EVERY VALUE MUST MAP rule above,
        naming it would assert it is reachable.

        ⚠ THE MAPPING TABLE AND <description> ARE UPDATED IN THE SAME EDIT, so the two do not drift
        from the formula. The remaining "Not Sent" bucket sources are Prepare, Approved, Not Sent
        (legacy) and Pending.

        ⚠ ONE THING THIS FIELD CANNOT REPRESENT AS OF THIS CHANGE: Disposition_NDA now has NO
        record-type default, so a UI-created NDA arrives with Status__c BLANK. TEXT() of a blank
        picklist is "", which matches no CASE branch and therefore takes the "Not Sent" fallback -
        the fail-CLOSED result this field was designed for, and correct here (an unsent document).
        It does mean a blank Status__c and a Prepare Status__c are INDISTINGUISHABLE on this field;
        anything that needs to tell them apart must read Status__c itself.

        READ-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION - a formula field cannot be edited directly, so FLS grants for
        this field must never set <editable>true</editable> anywhere; only <readable>. Granted on
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit and DPEG_Disposition_View (see those permission sets' own NDA__c
        blocks) since this is a disposition-facing display field. A Metadata API deployed field
        carries NO FLS for anyone, System Administrator included, so without those grants this
        field renders blank and any SOQL selecting it reports "No such column".
    -->
    <fullName>Tracking_Status__c</fullName>
    <description>Four-step display collapse of Status__c: Prepare/Approved/Not Sent/Pending -&gt; Not Sent; Sent/Received -&gt; Sent (Received maps to Sent deliberately - see XML comment); Signed -&gt; Signed; Declined -&gt; Declined. Explicit fallback of &apos;Not Sent&apos; for any future Status__c value not yet named here. Read-only; derived from Status__c.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <formula>CASE(
  TEXT(Status__c),
  &quot;Prepare&quot;, &quot;Not Sent&quot;,
  &quot;Approved&quot;, &quot;Not Sent&quot;,
  &quot;Not Sent&quot;, &quot;Not Sent&quot;,
  &quot;Pending&quot;, &quot;Not Sent&quot;,
  &quot;Sent&quot;, &quot;Sent&quot;,
  &quot;Received&quot;, &quot;Sent&quot;,
  &quot;Signed&quot;, &quot;Signed&quot;,
  &quot;Declined&quot;, &quot;Declined&quot;,
  &quot;Not Sent&quot;
)</formula>
    <inlineHelpText>Simplified display status derived from Status. Collapses the full lifecycle to Not Sent, Sent, Signed or Declined.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Tracking Status</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Text</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
